Title: Rooftop

[[rdg
Tone: Standoff
Start: Vance corners Marcus on the roof, convinced he leaked confidential files.
End: Marcus hands over his passkey and reveals that he was protecting his sister.
]]

[[character: Agent Vance
Voice: Controlled, precise. Asks questions already knowing the answer.
Want: Recover the files before anyone else sees them.
Obstacle: Marcus is the only person who knows where the backup is.
]]

[[character: Marcus
Voice: Defensive humor that cracks under pressure.
Want: Get his sister safely out of the city.
Obstacle: Vance is blocking the only exit.
]]

EXT. HIGH-RISE ROOFTOP — RAINY NIGHT

Rain ticks against a ventilation duct. MARCUS keeps one hand in his coat. VANCE watches that hand.

AGENT VANCE
The lift is locked.

MARCUS
I noticed. Very welcoming building.

AGENT VANCE
Take your hand out. Slowly.

Marcus produces a small plastic passkey. He holds it over the edge.

MARCUS
There’s a car downstairs. Blue. Engine running.

AGENT VANCE
Your driver can wait.

MARCUS
She’s fourteen. She can’t drive.

Vance lowers the radio without switching it on.

AGENT VANCE
Who else knows she’s there?

MARCUS
Everyone I stole those files from.

He sets the passkey on the duct between them. Neither reaches for it.
